# Build output (Rust). The V0 prototype lives in fsp-check/, the v0.x development crate in
# umbral/. Each keeps its own target directory: fsp-check/ is deliberately excluded from the
# Cargo workspace so its frozen build is unchanged.
/fsp-check/target/
target/

# Local scratch directories used to run the test suite on a second filesystem.
/.umbral-fsmatrix-tmp/

# PRIVATE — guard rule. A bundle of the pre-rewrite history would contain the private
# charter; if such a backup is ever created here, it must never be committed. The backup
# created during the sanitization was deleted from the working directory before publication.
/.sanitization-backup/

# Internal working record — the owner's publication checklist. Kept on disk, not published.
/PUBLICATION-PROPOSAL.md

# PRIVATE — must never be published.
# The project owner's founding charter is a private document, deliberately not part of
# the public edition; see README.md ("Naming and sources"). Do not remove this rule, and
# do not re-add the file.
/research/sources/PROJECT-MASTER-CONTEXT.md

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Operating system noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Local logs and scratch output that must never be committed
*.local.log
*.tmp
/tmp/

# Local environment and secrets. The repository must never contain credentials;
# these patterns exist so an accidental local file cannot be committed.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
credentials*
secrets*
